    {
      "id": 463,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -190.16287288025222,
        2795.8162701106035
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        620
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Model links",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS-Image SFT (Turbo) - Text to Image\n\n[MOSS-Image](https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-SFT) by the OpenMOSS Team, using the ComfyUI build from [Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image). Fast local text-to-image - about **5-10 seconds** for a 1024x1024 on this setup, quicker than Qwen-Image 2.1.\n\nThis workflow loads the **8-step turbo DMD LoRA by default**, so you get turbo speed out of the box. It reuses the Qwen text-encode node (it still works for MOSS) and adds a 2x upscale.\n\n### Models\n**diffusion_models**\n- [moss_image_sft_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/diffusion_models) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (default)\n\n**text_encoders** (set CLIPLoader type = `moss_image`)\n- [qwen3.5_9b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/` (standard)\n- [qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/` (further quantized, lower VRAM - runs on 6-8 GB)\n\n**vae**\n- [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/vae) -> `models/vae/` (MOSS uses the Flux 2 VAE)\n\n**loras (8-step turbo DMD, by lodestones)**\n- [lora_latest.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/lodestones/MOSS-Image-SFT-8-steps-dmd/tree/main) -> `models/loras/` (**loaded by default**; `_latest` = newest checkpoint)\n- [lora.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/lodestones/MOSS-Image-SFT-8-steps-dmd/tree/main) -> `models/loras/` (alternate)\n\n### Settings\nKSampler: **8 steps, cfg 1, sampler euler_ancestral, scheduler simple.** With the 8-step LoRA you don't need to raise steps.\n\n### GGUF (not working yet - left in for later)\nThe **GGUF loader group is bypassed on purpose.** The standard ComfyUI-GGUF (city96) `UnetLoaderGGUF` node does **not** support the MOSS-Image architecture yet - it expects a `moss_image` marker the stock node can't read. GGUF quants do exist ([realrebelai/MOSS-Image_GGUFs](https://huggingface.co/realrebelai/MOSS-Image_GGUFs)) but currently need an experimental MOSS-specific bridge node. I've left the GGUF group in so it's ready the moment native support lands - until then, use the int8 diffusion model above (pair it with the w4a8 encoder for low VRAM).\n\n### Custom nodes\n- rgthree-comfy (Any Switch, Fast Groups Bypasser)\n- ComfyUI-GGUF (for the future GGUF path)\n\nUpdate ComfyUI to the latest - MOSS-Image support is in recent builds. MOSS-Image by the OpenMOSS Team; 8-step turbo LoRA by lodestones."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MOSS-Image SFT (Turbo) - Text to Image\n\n[MOSS-Image](https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-SFT) by the OpenMOSS Team, using the ComfyUI build from [Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image). Fast local text-to-image - about **5-10 seconds** for a 1024x1024 on this setup, quicker than Qwen-Image 2.1.\n\nThis workflow loads the **8-step turbo DMD LoRA by default**, so you get turbo speed out of the box. It reuses the Qwen text-encode node (it still works for MOSS) and adds a 2x upscale.\n\n### Models\n**diffusion_models**\n- [moss_image_sft_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/diffusion_models) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (default)\n\n**text_encoders** (set CLIPLoader type = `moss_image`)\n- [qwen3.5_9b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/` (standard)\n- [qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/` (further quantized, lower VRAM - runs on 6-8 GB)\n\n**vae**\n- [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/tree/main/vae) -> `models/vae/` (MOSS uses the Flux 2 VAE)\n\n**loras (8-step turbo DMD, by lodestones)**\n- [lora_latest.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/lodestones/MOSS-Image-SFT-8-steps-dmd/tree/main) -> `models/loras/` (**loaded by default**; `_latest` = newest checkpoint)\n- [lora.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/lodestones/MOSS-Image-SFT-8-steps-dmd/tree/main) -> `models/loras/` (alternate)\n\n### Settings\nKSampler: **8 steps, cfg 1, sampler euler_ancestral, scheduler simple.** With the 8-step LoRA you don't need to raise steps.\n\n### GGUF (not working yet - left in for later)\nThe **GGUF loader group is bypassed on purpose.** The standard ComfyUI-GGUF (city96) `UnetLoaderGGUF` node does **not** support the MOSS-Image architecture yet - it expects a `moss_image` marker the stock node can't read. GGUF quants do exist ([realrebelai/MOSS-Image_GGUFs](https://huggingface.co/realrebelai/MOSS-Image_GGUFs)) but currently need an experimental MOSS-specific bridge node. I've left the GGUF group in so it's ready the moment native support lands - until then, use the int8 diffusion model above (pair it with the w4a8 encoder for low VRAM).\n\n### Custom nodes\n- rgthree-comfy (Any Switch, Fast Groups Bypasser)\n- ComfyUI-GGUF (for the future GGUF path)\n\nUpdate ComfyUI to the latest - MOSS-Image support is in recent builds. MOSS-Image by the OpenMOSS Team; 8-step turbo LoRA by lodestones."
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
